---
// Two of the three labels here used to point at pages the build does not emit: `dist/client` contains
// index.html, chat/index.html and 404.html only, and public/ has no redirect rules — so "Schedule" and
// "Members" rendered the 404 page in production, on main as well as here. The operator ruled: drop them.
//
// What the row costs now (measured by `npm run check:render`, which prints needed-of-available at every
// width it runs): the mark plus Chat needs **171px**, against a container that offers 276 at a 320
// viewport and 256 even at 300. That is why the narrow type tier went away — see
// --breakpoint-nav-narrow's retirement in src/styles/global.css and D117: with this label set the wide
// tier fits everywhere, so a second tier bought nothing.
//
// Headroom, measured before the schedule page existed: "Schedule" is 57.6px at this tier, so adding it
// back puts the row at 245 (171 + a 16px gap + 57.6) — inside 276. A third link would not fit at the
// floor. So the row carries ONE more real path, not two, and the probe says so the moment it does not.
// 2026-11-07: that one path is spent on `Schedule`, because `src/pages/schedule.astro` now emits
// `dist/client/schedule/index.html` (D117's rule — a label needs a page behind it, and this is the page
// the homepage's next-date card points at). `Members` stays out: there is still no members page, and the
// arithmetic says a third label would clip at the 320 floor anyway.
const navItems = [
  { href: '/schedule', label: 'Schedule' },
  { href: '/chat', label: 'Chat' },
];
---

<header class="bg-paper">
  <nav class="max-w-screen-xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-4">
    <!-- D100 shape B, re-measured on the built artifact by `npm run check:render`: one row at every
         width, `flex-wrap: nowrap`, one type tier (text-label) at every width, 16px gaps, and link
         targets 32px tall (16px line box + py-2). D100 rejected a 13px target, so the pad is
         load-bearing — do not shave it.

         `flex-nowrap` is the load-bearing part. The shipped nav was `flex-col` + `flex-wrap`, which is
         why the page clipped and links disappeared (A needed 397px, more than every content box this
         site ships). With nowrap, a label set that stops fitting shows up as a failed width probe
         instead of a silent re-wrap. -->
    <div class="flex flex-nowrap items-center gap-4">
      <a
        href="/"
        class="flex-shrink-0 whitespace-nowrap py-2 font-body text-body text-ink"
        aria-label="Minneapolis Math Book Club, home"
      >
        MPLS <em class="not-italic text-gold">Math</em> Club
      </a>
      <div class="flex flex-nowrap items-center gap-4">
        {navItems.map(item => (
          <a
            href={item.href}
            class="whitespace-nowrap py-2 text-label text-ink font-medium hover:text-gold"
            aria-label={`Navigate to ${item.label}`}
          >
            {item.label}
          </a>
        ))}
      </div>
    </div>
  </nav>
</header>
